# Abstract
# --------
# GitHub requests a review from the code owners automatically when a pull
# request touches a matching path, and branch protection can require their
# approval before a merge. Each line pairs a gitignore-style pattern with one
# or more owners. When several patterns match a file, the last matching line
# in this file wins, so the catch-all pattern comes first and the specific
# paths follow it. A trailing `#` on a pattern line would be read as part of
# the owner list, so every comment stands on its own line above the entry.
# =============================================================================

# Default owner for every file not matched by a later, more specific pattern.
